        <title type="html"><![CDATA[hyphenate-limit-chars: list auto and <integer> as separate values]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45854</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45854"/>
        <updated>2026-09-26T09:27:00.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236759479?u=6a2b51441b1015f9a4beae865bfcb3f1a2ea9899&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">The Values section listed the one-, two- and three-value combinations of <code class="notranslate">&lt;number&gt;</code> and explained <code class="notranslate">auto</code> in a paragraph below them. This lists <code class="notranslate">auto</code> and <code class="notranslate">&lt;integer&gt;</code> as the two entries, with the position rules (and what an omitted second or third value becomes) under <code class="notranslate">&lt;integer&gt;</code>, as suggested in the review of <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4992022479" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44937" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/44937/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44937">#44937</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">It also changes <code class="notranslate">&lt;number&gt;</code> to <code class="notranslate">&lt;integer&gt;</code>: the spec grammar is <code class="notranslate">[ auto | &lt;integer [0,∞]&gt; ]{1,3}</code>, and non-integers are rejected.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">auto</code> was the only value not in the definition list, and <code class="notranslate">&lt;number&gt;</code> suggested that values like <code class="notranslate">1.5</code> are allowed.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Spec: <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-4/#propdef-hyphenate-limit-chars" rel="nofollow">CSS Text 4, <code class="notranslate">hyphenate-limit-chars</code></a> ("If the third value is missing, it is the same as the second. If the second value is missing, then it is auto.")</li>
<li>WPT <a href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-text/parsing/hyphenate-limit-chars-invalid.html"><code class="notranslate">hyphenate-limit-chars-invalid.html</code></a> treats <code class="notranslate">1.2</code>, <code class="notranslate">1 1.2</code> and <code class="notranslate">1 2 1.2</code> as invalid.</li>
<li>Checked in headless Edge 153 with <code class="notranslate">CSS.supports("hyphenate-limit-chars", …)</code>: <code class="notranslate">10</code>, <code class="notranslate">10 4</code>, <code class="notranslate">10 4 4</code>, <code class="notranslate">auto 3</code>, <code class="notranslate">10 auto 4</code> are true; <code class="notranslate">1.2</code>, <code class="notranslate">10.0</code>, <code class="notranslate">10 4.5</code>, <code class="notranslate">10 4 4.5</code> are false.</li>
<li>markdownlint-cli2, prettier and cspell pass on the file.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #45071.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5112357853" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45071" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/45071/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45071">#45071</a></p>]]></content>
